= The Eberlein Plan

Hugo Eberlein, sent by the Zentrale to Central Germany, has a plan to make the workers angry enough to come out. Bombs at railway lines and munitions trains. Perhaps a staged attack on our own offices, or the faked kidnapping of a party leader, to be blamed on the right.

He says the masses need a shock. Some members of the Zentrale do not want to know the details.

- @approve: Approve it.
- @forbid: Forbid it outright.
- @remove: Forbid it, and recall Eberlein.

@approve
subtitle: The Left's logic, carried to its end. If it comes out, it will poison everything.
on-arrival: e21_ma_eberlein = 1; crisis_momentum += 4; repression += 6; luxemburgist_satisfaction -= 12; unionist_satisfaction -= 6; offensive_satisfaction += 2; lean_offensive += 1

A few bombs go off in the week that follows. A railway bridge is damaged. Nobody believes the right did it.

@forbid
subtitle: The Spartacist line: we do not deceive the workers.
on-arrival: luxemburgist_satisfaction += 5; lean_luxemburgist += 1

The Zentrale forbids it. Eberlein shrugs and goes back to organising the fighting groups.

@remove
subtitle: The Spartacists and the Right together. The Left calls it weakness.
on-arrival: luxemburgist_satisfaction += 6; unionist_satisfaction += 4; offensive_satisfaction -= 5; unity -= 2; lean_luxemburgist += 1; lean_unionist += 1

Eberlein is recalled to Berlin and his plan goes into the Zentrale's safe. It will not stay secret forever.
